  <content>
    <section>
      <title>Cool Down Activity</title>
      <para><term class="glossary-tooltip"> Functions</term> \(R\) and \(D\) give the height, in feet, of a toy rocket and a drone, \(t\) seconds after they are released. Here are the graphs of \(R\) (for the rocket) and \(D\) (for the drone).</para>
      <para>
        <figure>
          <media alt="Two functions graphed on a cooridnate plane.">
            <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_13_12_01.svg"/>
          </media>
        </figure>
     </para>
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>Which of the inequalities is true: \(R(2)&gt;D(2)\) or \(D(2)&gt; R(2)\)?</para>
          <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>\(R(2)&gt;D(2)\)</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>What was the height of the drone when the toy rocket hit the ground?</para>
          <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>20 feet</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>For what value of \(t\) is \(R(t)=D(t)\) true?</para>
          <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>About \(t=4.5\).</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para> What does this tell you about the drone and the toy rocket?</para>
          <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>After 4.5 seconds, the toy rocket and the drone are at the same height.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
    </section>
  </content>
